# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Cloudflare Pages / Netlify redirects
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  There is deliberately no `/*  /index.html  200` catch-all any more.
#
#  It was there when this really was a single page with anchor navigation, and it
#  was harmless then. With seven real case-study routes it stopped being a safety
#  net and became a way to hide breakage: a mistyped or stale `/project/...` path
#  would serve the overview with a 200 instead of failing, and the client would
#  render the homepage because the document it received has no `data-project`
#  attribute. A wrong page, returned as a success, to a crawler and to a person
#  alike.
#
#  Every route on this site is a real file, so an unmatched path *should* 404.
#  `404.html` handles it, and it lists all seven systems so a dead link still
#  ends somewhere useful.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Legacy shape from the pre-routes version, so an old bookmark or a link pasted
# into a hiring thread months ago still resolves to the real page rather than
# hitting the 404. Scoped to the one known file instead of being a general rule,
# because a general rule is the thing that was removed above.
/project.html?id=llm-drift-monitor   /project/llm-drift-monitor/            301
/project.html?id=from-scratch-to-served  /project/from-scratch-to-served/  301
